// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 19-concurrency
// facility: rule.conc.spawn [Thread-Lend]; spec/18 contained; D-0240; CHG-0304; conf.thread-holding-guard-contained
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.aliasing-conflict (dynamic)
// expect-stdout-hex: 6265666f7265206a6f696e0a
//
// The thread's closure owns the guard `g`, whose lock path is `main`'s and is
// not lent (D-0240): the thread's write through it faults. Holding a lock path
// does not make the thread lent, so its fault is contained: `main` goes on and
// prints, and the failure is raised again at `join`. cobc counted the lock
// path as lent and ended the program at once (CHG-0304).

import std;

fn main()
{
    mutex<i32> m = Mutex::new(0);
    auto g = lock(&m);
    auto t = spawn(move [g]() { *g = *g + 1; });
    printf("before join\n");
    join(t);
}
